# Git stores every text file with LF line ends and checks it out with LF on
# every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says. The release scripts and the
# tools read these files byte for byte, and a CR breaks them. `cargo xtask
# check-repo` rejects a file committed with CRLF line ends (rule line-endings).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files, stored and checked out byte for byte.
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.gif binary
*.gz binary
*.ico binary
*.jpeg binary
*.jpg binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.tar binary
*.ttf binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
